infographic compare-quadrant-quarter-simple-card
data
  title Match the abstraction to your traffic shape
  desc Two axes decide it: direction (server→client vs bidirectional) and HTTP fit (plain proxy-friendly HTTP vs a protocol switch / HTTP-2-only).
  compares
    - label One-way · plain HTTP → SSE
      desc Server pushes, client listens. text/event-stream rides any proxy with no upgrade and auto-reconnects. Live dashboards, notifications, AI token streams.
    - label One-way · streamed body → Chunked transfer
      desc Transfer-Encoding chunked sends size-prefixed chunks before the total length is known. Generated HTML, log tailing. HTTP/2+ does this natively via DATA frames.
    - label Bidirectional · protocol switch → WebSocket
      desc 101 Switching Protocols ends HTTP and opens a binary frame tunnel either side may write to. Chat, collaborative editing, multiplayer. RFC 8441 brings it onto HTTP/2.
    - label Bidirectional · HTTP/2-only → gRPC
      desc Protobuf RPCs multiplex as HTTP/2 streams; status lands in trailers, invisible to HTTP monitoring. gRPC-Web proxies rewrite trailers into the body for browsers.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
